= The Battle for the USPD

The USPD delegates came home from Moscow divided. Däumig and Stoecker want to accept the conditions. Crispien and Dittmann call them a dictatorship, and Hilferding writes in *Freiheit* that they would hand the German movement over to the Russian state. Every USPD branch is voting, one by one, before the party congress at Halle in October. [? if e20_cond_dir = 1 : Zinoviev's telegram says the Executive will judge the German section by the result. ?]

In Italy four hundred thousand metalworkers have occupied their factories.

- @quiet: Work with Däumig, Stoecker and Koenen, and say little in public.
- @attack: Attack Crispien, Dittmann and Hilferding by name.
- @factories: Run common strike committees with the USPD's workers.

@quiet
subtitle: The USPD left will lead its own members to us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.comply(15);
!}

In Halle-Merseburg and Berlin the USPD left wins branch after branch.

@attack
subtitle: The most radical Independents will rally. The rest will be frightened.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_attacked = 1;
Q.uspd_relation -= 10;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
RG.comply(30);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
!}

*Die Rote Fahne* calls the USPD right agents of the bourgeoisie. The left wins votes in the cities. In the small towns the members rally to the old leaders.

@factories
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Workers who strike together will vote together.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids common struggles with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.uspd_relation += 8;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
RG.comply(15);
!}

At Leuna and in the Berlin machine shops our cells and the USPD's strike together over the price of bread.
